---
description: Finish one wave of sub-agents before launching the next
alwaysApply: true
---

# Sub-agent waves

Launch one wave, then wait. Do not start the next wave until every sub-agent in the current wave has finished.

- A wave is the set of sub-agents started together. After that launch, stop. Do not call Task again for more agents in the same turn or in later turns until those agents report completion.
- A launch that returns "Too many local subagents" did not start. Do not resume that id. Do not fill the gap with another wave. Those tasks belong in a later wave, after the current one is done.
- End the turn after starting a wave so completion notices can arrive. Do not poll or sleep-wait on the agents.
- When the wave finishes, review its edits, then start the next disjoint wave.

```text
# Bad: wave 2 starts while wave 1 is still running
Task(wave1-a); Task(wave1-b); Task(wave2-a)

# Good: wave 2 waits for both completions
Task(wave1-a); Task(wave1-b)
# ...both agents finish...
Task(wave2-a)
```
